# lahn course: written by the course tools (tools/courses; change it there, and run them again)
version 2
title Reading music
description From your first note on the staff to reading melodies to a beat, in every key: a note or two at a time.
instrument bass


level The G string

chapter The G string: G
page
  block text
    text Music is written on five lines, the staff. The higher a note sits, the higher it sounds. Bass music is written in the bass clef, the curl with two dots, and sounds an octave lower than written.
    text G sits in the top space. On the bass it's the open G string.
  block staff
    notes G2/1
  block fretboard
    frets 0 4
    lit 4:0
  block heading
    text Rhythm: the beat
  block text
    text A filled note with a stem is a **quarter note**: it lasts one beat. Tap your foot evenly and count 1 2 3 4, a note on each count.
  block staff
    notes G2 G2 G2 G2
